LESSON 5: PHOTO EDITING & RETOUCHING
================================================================

WHAT YOU'LL DO
--------------
Edit photos for individuals, families, or small business owners.
Good photo editing can make a product look more appealing, a
portrait more flattering, or a business's images look polished
and professional.

----------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 1: WHAT PHOTO EDITING GIGS LOOK LIKE
----------------------------------------------------------------
Clients give you their raw or unedited photos and you make them
look better. Common requests include:

  - Adjusting brightness, contrast, and color
  - Removing blemishes from portraits
  - Removing or replacing backgrounds
  - Making product photos look clean and consistent
  - Applying a consistent filter or style to a set of photos

Clients include small business owners (product photos for Etsy
or Instagram), families (portraits from events), real estate
agents (property photos), and social media creators.

----------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 2: FREE TOOLS
----------------------------------------------------------------
Snapseed (mobile app)
  Simple and powerful. Great for basic edits: brightness,
  contrast, color, sharpening. Easy to use on your phone.

Lightroom Mobile (mobile app, free version)
  More advanced. Good for color grading and applying consistent
  styles across multiple photos. Free version is plenty to start.

Photopea (photopea.com)
  Browser-based tool that works like Photoshop. Free. Best for
  background removal and more detailed retouching.

----------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 3: BASIC EDITS EVERY CLIENT EXPECTS
----------------------------------------------------------------
Brightness and exposure
  Make sure the photo isn't too dark or too bright. This is
  the most common issue with phone photos taken indoors.

Contrast
  Adjusting contrast makes colors pop and the image feel crisper.
  Too much looks harsh; too little looks flat.

Background removal
  Very common for product photos. Clients selling on Etsy, Amazon,
  or their website often want clean white backgrounds.
  Use Photopea or a free tool like Remove.bg.

Blemish removal
  For portrait photos, clients may want minor skin blemishes
  removed. Use the healing tool in Snapseed or Photopea.

Color correction
  Fix photos that look too warm (orange/yellow) or too cool (blue).
  This often happens with indoor lighting.

----------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 4: WHAT CLIENTS ASK FOR MOST
----------------------------------------------------------------
  Product photos    — White background, sharp focus, accurate colors.
                      Used for online stores and social media.

  Portraits         — Flattering light, clear skin, bright eyes.
                      Used for headshots, family photos, events.

  Real estate       — Bright, wide, neutral. Rooms should look spacious.
                      Fixing dark windows is a common request.

  Instagram sets    — A series of photos with a consistent style
                      or filter. Clients want them to look like a
                      cohesive feed.

----------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 5: HOW TO DELIVER EDITED FILES
----------------------------------------------------------------
  Format     — JPEG for most uses. PNG if they need transparency.
  Resolution — Deliver at the original resolution unless asked
               for something smaller for web use.
  Method     — Google Drive or Dropbox for large files.
               Email works for 1-3 photos.

Always send a Google Drive or Dropbox folder link when delivering
more than 3 photos. Name your files clearly (e.g., "photo_01_edited.jpg").

----------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 6: HOW TO PRICE YOUR WORK
----------------------------------------------------------------
Starting rates:

  Basic edit (brightness, contrast, color):   $3–$8 per photo
  Background removal:                          $5–$15 per photo
  Full retouch (blemish removal, color, etc.): $10–$25 per photo
  Batch editing (10+ photos, same style):      Offer a package rate,
                                               e.g., $50 for 10 photos

----------------------------------------------------------------
MINI PROJECT
----------------------------------------------------------------
Find or take 3 photos (you can use your own or download free stock
photos from Unsplash.com).

Edit each one and create a before/after comparison:
  - Adjust brightness and contrast
  - Correct the color temperature
  - Remove the background on at least one photo

Save both the original and edited version side by side.
This is your portfolio sample.

